# Day 26 - What Deployment Means

##  Learning Objectives

- Learned what deployment means.
- Understood how GitHub Pages publishes websites.
- Learned why proofreading is important before publishing.

## What is Deployment?

Deployment is the process of publishing a website from a local computer to the internet so other people can access it.

## Deployment Flow

VS Code
↓
GitHub Repository
↓
GitHub Pages
↓
Live Website

## Practical Work

- Reviewed all website text.
- Corrected spelling and capitalization.
- Checked headings, buttons, and links.

## Key Takeaways

- Deployment makes a website publicly available.
- Proofreading improves professionalism and user experience.
